Product Catalog Microservice
----------------------------
Our Product Catalog microservice is responsible for retrieving product information from a database and return it to the client

For example, when a customer opens an e-commerce website, they might see:
- Laptop — ₹50,000
- Mobile — ₹20,000
- Headphones — ₹2,000
The Product Catalog microservice provides this information.

Technologies used : 
| Component            |          Purpose    |

Node.js	                Executes our JavaScript application
Express.js            	Creates REST API endpoints
MongoDB	                Stores product information
MongoDB Driver          Allows Node.js to communicate with MongoDB
index.js                Main application file
products.json         	Contains initial product information
package.json     	Defines application dependencies
Docker	                Packages the application into a container
Port 3001              	Exposes the Product Catalog API


Understanding the API endpoints:

Endpoin                  t	Purpose
GET /api/products	Returns all products
GET /api/products/:id	Returns a specific product
GET /health/live	Checks whether the application is running
GET /health/ready	Checks whether the application can communicate with MongoDB

Step-by-step explanation
Step 1: Customer requests products
The customer opens the products page of the e-commerce website.
The frontend sends an HTTP request:
GET /api/products

Step 2: Product Catalog receives the request
Express.js receives the request on port 3001.
It identifies the matching API endpoint.

Step 3: Application queries MongoDB
The application uses the MongoDB driver to communicate with the database.
It requests all documents from the products collection.

Step 4: MongoDB retrieves the data
MongoDB searches the collection and returns the available product records.

Step 5: Product Catalog sends the response
The application converts the result into a JSON HTTP response.

Step 6: Frontend displays the products
The frontend receives the JSON data and displays the product information to the customer.


