After writing the docker file for this test the system by running these thhings:

First create a docker network: 
>> docker network create ecommerce-net

Create a persistent volume: 
>> docker volume create ecommerce-mongo-data

for the mongodb to store the data when so that the data remain persistant

Start the monogDB:
>> docker run -d \
  --name ecommerce-mongo \
  --network ecommerce-net \
  -v ecommerce-mongo-data:/data/db \
  mongo:6.0

Run the microservice : 
docker run -d \
  --name product-catalog \
  --network ecommerce-net \
  -p 3001:3001 \
  -e PORT=3001 \
  -e MONGODB_HOST=ecommerce-mongo \
  -e MONGODB_PORT=27017 \
  -e MONGODB_DATABASE=products_db \
  product-catalog:v1



Test the application: 

check the containers: 
>> docker ps

Check the product catalogs: 
>> docker logs product-catalog

response: 
Connected to MongoDB
Initial products inserted
Product Catalog running on port 3001

Test the liveness:
>> curl http://localhost:3001/health/live

response: 
{
  "status": "alive",
  "service": "product-catalog"
}

test the readiness: 
>> curl http://localhost:3001/health/ready

response: 
{
  "status": "ready",
  "database": "connected"
}

test graceful shutdown:
>> docker stop product-catalog
>> docker logs --tail 15 product-catalog

expected message: 
>>
Received SIGTERM. Shutting down...
Graceful shutdown completed



