create the kubernetes directories: 

cd ~/production-ecommerce-k8s

mkdir -p infrastructure/kubernetes/base/product-catalog
mkdir -p infrastructure/kubernetes/databases/mongodb


* base/product-catalog/ will contain the Kubernetes configuration for the Product Catalog application.
* databases/mongodb/ will contain MongoDB's configuration and persistent storage resources.




for the persistant storage of the  data of the mongo db we need to create the pvc in the minikube there is no need of specifing the storage class 

but in amazon eks  we must create the storageclassfirst:

>> storageclass.yaml

apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass

metadata:
  name: gp3

provisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com

parameters:
  type: gp3
  encrypted: "true"

volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer  # it delays volume provisioning untile kubernetes know where the pod can be scheduled so that i can create the volume in the same az as the pod or worker node

reclaimPolicy: Retain      # this tells what will  happen to the volume when the  pvc is deleted


allowVolumeExpansion: true  # this allows you to increase the pvc's requested storage capacity later



Important: A PDB does not prevent hardware failures, pod crashes, or every type of deletion. It primarily protects against voluntary disruptions that use the Kubernetes Eviction API.
